[00:08.41]A: I used to rule the world
[00:12.10]B: Seas would rise when I gave the word
[00:14.58]A: Now in the morning, I sleep alone
[00:18.90]B: Sweep the streets I used to own
[00:35.89]A: I used to roll the dice
[00:39.95]B: Feel the fear in my enemy's eyes
[00:43.21]A: Listened as the crowd would sing
[00:47.02]AB: "Now the old king is dead, long live the king"
[00:49.86]A: One minute I held the key
[00:53.83]B: Next, the walls were closed on me
[00:56.50]A: And I discovered that my castles stand
[01:00.76]B: Upon pillars of salt and pillars of sand
[01:04.58]AB: I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[01:08.46]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[01:11.92]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[01:15.04]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[01:18.84]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[01:22.24]B: Once you'd gone, there was never
[01:24.87]A: Never an honest word
[01:28.58]AB: And that was when I ruled the world
[01:45.23]A: It was a wicked and wild wind
[01:49.40]B: Blew down the doors to let me in
[01:52.09]A: Shattered windows and the sound of drums
[01:56.45]B: People couldn't believe what I'd become
[01:59.64]A: Revolutionaries wait
[02:03.48]B: For my head on a silver plate
[02:05.93]A: Just a puppet on a lonely string
[02:10.50]B: Oh, who would ever want to be king?
[02:14.27]AB: I hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[02:17.87]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[02:21.28]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[02:24.74]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[02:28.22]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[02:31.80]B: I know Saint Peter won't call my name
[02:34.99]A: Never an honest word
[02:38.06]AB: But that was when I ruled the world
[03:10.40]AB: Hear Jerusalem bells a-ringing
[03:13.45]AB: Roman cavalry choirs are singing
[03:17.03]AB: Be my mirror, my sword and shield
[03:20.31]AB: My missionaries in a foreign field
[03:23.93]A: For some reason, I can't explain
[03:27.39]B: I know Saint Peter won't call my name
[03:30.53]A: Never an honest word
[03:33.77]AB: But that was when I ruled the world
